WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.240
Hi, I'm Soffit!

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:05.723
Here is how one small change to an activation helps a

00:00:05.723 --> 00:00:06.989
network draw sharp edges.

00:00:09.183 --> 00:00:12.429
A coordinate network turns a position into a value.

00:00:12.429 --> 00:00:14.233
Earlier fixes chose its frequencies.

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:17.119
This one learns how each neuron mixes them.

00:00:18.858 --> 00:00:21.955
Fourier features, SIREN and FINER change the menu.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:26.213
Each neuron still emits one fixed waveform, welded to its feature.

00:00:26.633 --> 00:00:28.601
Here the weights still pick the feature.

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:31.131
A short list of learned numbers decides the waveform.

00:00:32.775 --> 00:00:33.899
Here is the formula.

00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:38.290
It starts as the identity, so the network begins almost linear.

00:00:38.710 --> 00:00:41.226
Then it adds whole-number harmonics of the same input.

00:00:41.757 --> 00:00:45.207
Each harmonic gets a learned amplitude, shared by the whole layer.

00:00:46.883 --> 00:00:50.334
A coordinate goes through the weights, which choose what this neuron looks at.

00:00:50.753 --> 00:00:54.038
The same value is fed to a bank of sines, one per harmonic.

00:00:54.458 --> 00:00:57.627
Learned amplitudes weight and sum them, so one neuron can make a

00:00:57.627 --> 00:00:58.947
square edge on its own.

00:00:59.367 --> 00:01:02.821
The output is linear in those amplitudes, so tuning the spectrum

00:01:02.821 --> 00:01:04.076
is a direct problem.

00:01:05.633 --> 00:01:09.473
In the paper's toy test, SIREN and FINER need more atoms to

00:01:09.473 --> 00:01:10.753
fit a wiggly signal.

00:01:11.173 --> 00:01:13.546
The learned harmonic unit fits it with one.

00:01:13.546 --> 00:01:16.215
The target suits it, so this shows the mechanism.

00:01:17.675 --> 00:01:21.967
On twenty four Kodak photos the paper reports about thirty eight decibels,

00:01:21.967 --> 00:01:25.187
just ahead of FINER and three ahead of SIREN.

00:01:26.258 --> 00:01:28.006
The parameters are almost free.

00:01:28.006 --> 00:01:32.899
The compute is not: a step takes nearly seven times as long as FINER's.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:37.993
The idea to keep: give each layer a learned recipe for mixing

00:01:37.993 --> 00:01:40.422
harmonics, and let the weights just pick features.

00:01:42.442 --> 00:01:43.366
Frequencies picked.

00:01:43.366 --> 00:01:44.290
Harmonics mixed.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.138
Better fits, slower steps.

00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:49.151
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:49.151 --> 00:01:49.754
I'm Soffit.

00:01:49.754 --> 00:01:50.055
Bye!
